Z||000002||Raydar||01-05-2001||09:57 AM||||The batwing company? I usta work for them too. Like ten years ago. No corporate conscience whatsoever, even then. They suck. All IMHO, of course. <P>Good luck in your search. <BR>How far are you from Richardson? There are all kinds of hi-tech firms there. I was at Alcatel for training. They looked like they might be a fun company to work for. Nortel might be interesting too, if you can get a foot in the door.<p>[This message has been edited by Raydar (edited 01-05-2001).]||||reg||13
Z||000003||LarryB||01-06-2001||12:59 AM||||Raydar, were you at Alcatel for DACS training or for some of their other network hardware? <P>JetroGT, if you have good basic electronics skills you might want to try to get a job as a transmission tech for one of the carriers like a WorldCom or Level 3 (avoid the Baby Bells).  Good ones are tough to come by so they're usually willing to train with good pay and job security. You'd see plenty of Alcatel, Nortel, and Fujitsu gear as well.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>And Dallas is a pretty important aggregation/peering point for long-haul telco. :<P>||||reg||6
